Spike #11 (PR #359) retrieved the arXiv:2401.03553 PDF via WebFetch +
pdftotext extraction and verified the actual authors are Finnian Gray
and David Kubizňák. The original literature review (dispatched as a
prior subagent task) misattributed it to Houri-Tanahashi-Yasui 2024 in
four locations:

  - §1 Summary (line 13): commuting-operator-tower citation
  - §2c (line 32): scalar/vector/tensor extension citation
  - §3 Most Load-Bearing Papers, row 7 (line 67): full table entry
  - §4 Gap 1 (line 84): Casimir-of-commuting-operator-algebra citation

All four corrected to Gray-Kubizňák 2024.

Note on paper title + journal ref: the original lit review entry
(row 7 of the table) claimed the paper title "Homogeneous Symmetry
Operators in Kerr-NUT-AdS Spacetimes" and journal ref "Phys. Rev. D
109:084027". Spike #11's PDF extraction verified the AUTHORS and
arXiv ID, but did NOT independently verify the title or journal ref.
Both are now flagged for re-verification in the table row's
explanatory annotation; only the arXiv ID is treated as
direct-confirmed.

Per the project's Gemini-CLI-taint discipline: when a subagent
catches a factual error introduced by an earlier subagent, the
correction is part of the deliverable. Spike #11's verification
discipline (extract the paper, read it, don't trust attributions)
is the gold standard for citation hygiene going forward.

Cross-reference: §VII.4.1.2 of the MFO notebook (PR #360) also had
the misattribution; that fix is being merged separately.

