 ### Gap 1: Casimir of the principal-Killing-Yano commuting-operator algebra
-Houri-Tanahashi-Yasui 2024 (arXiv:2401.03553) gives 4 commuting operators for the scalar perturbation algebra on Kerr-NUT-(A)dS, all polynomial in the principal CKY tensor. **No published work writes down a quadratic (or higher) combination of these operators and identifies it as a Casimir whose eigenvalue formula closes the QNM spectrum.** This is the most direct analog of the CMS Casimir construction.
